  abstract = {Software engineering practices known as DevOps seek to integrate software development (Dev) and software operation (Ops). The purpose of this study was to focus on how the DevOps methodologies are to shorten the life cycle of development and provide consistent production of high-quality software. Software developers and IT operations specialists are encouraged to work together, communicate, and integrate using the DevOps methodology. Organizations can provide apps and services more rapidly and dependably using this method. Agile software development, which aims to reduce development cycles and give clients more regular updates, benefits greatly from DevOps, application deployment using the DevOps methodology. Applications are made, run, and maintained in a quality way at all stages. The tooling being used building, testing, and deploying processes will move to the cloud as more firms adopt DevOps, essentially turning continuous delivery into a regulated remote server. An innovative model in business applications is DevOps-as-a-Service. Using scalable digital developer tools, DevOps-as-a-Service shifts the typical interaction between the production and operational teams to the cloud. The organizational structure must undergo a significant change in order to transition from a traditional mindset to an agile mindset. Adopting such a culture involves a range of strategies and levels of involvement. In this study, we discuss adoption concepts, adoption tactics, and their effects.},
